 "summary": "Adds python-setuptools as a native input for Python packages in the Guix codesign manifest and patches certvalidator's test phase to use standard unittest discovery. This works around breaking changes introduced by Python 3.12, which stopped bundling setuptools and removed the deprecated imp module.",
 "problem": "The macOS codesigning environment fails to build under Guix using Python 3.12 because setuptools is missing and certvalidator's custom test runner imports the removed imp module.",
 "evidence": [
  "Linked issue #36421 reports 'guix: python-setuptools missing from codesign manifest after python 3.12'",
  "Commit 82a8c8009a notes: 'Certvalidator's custom test runner imports imp and fails before running any tests, preventing the macOS codesigning environment from building.'"
 ],
